# Auth

Clerk is the only authentication system. Do not add another auth library, custom
passwords, session cookies, or JWT handling.

Session UI and route protection stay on the Clerk helpers already in the app:
`ClerkProvider` in [app/layout.tsx](mdc:app/layout.tsx) and `clerkMiddleware` in
[proxy.ts](mdc:proxy.ts). Sign-in and sign-up open in a Clerk modal from
shadcn `Button` components, as required by
[.cursor/rules/shadcn-ui.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/shadcn-ui.mdc). Do not mount
`<SignIn />` or `<SignUp />` as the control that starts auth.

This app has no sign-in page. Do not add a `/sign-in` route, do not set
`signInUrl` to one, and do not `redirect` a signed-out user there.

## Protected pages

A page that requires a session reads `userId` from `auth()`. When `userId` is
missing, `redirect` to `/`. The homepage is where the sign-in and sign-up
buttons live. Do not send that visitor to a sign-in page.

## Whose data

On the server, in Server Components, Server Actions, and Route Handlers, the
signed-in user comes only from `auth()` in `@clerk/nextjs/server`:

```ts
const { userId } = await auth()
```

`userId` is the Clerk user id stored on `decks.userId` in
[src/db/schema.ts](mdc:src/db/schema.ts). Never take it from search params, form
data, headers, or a request body. A missing `userId` means the caller is signed
out: do not read or write `decks` or `cards`.

`cards` have no owner column. A card belongs to whoever owns its parent deck.
An id supplied by the client is not proof of ownership.

Every read and write must be scoped to that `userId`:

- `decks`: every `select`, `insert`, `update`, and `delete` includes
  `eq(decks.userId, userId)`. Inserts set `userId` to that same value.
- `cards`: before selecting, inserting, updating, or deleting a card, the
  parent deck must match both the deck id and `eq(decks.userId, userId)`.
- If the ownership check matches nothing, treat the row as not found. Do not
  fall back to a query by id alone.

The `"user_example"` value in [src/index.ts](mdc:src/index.ts) is seed data
only. Application code must not copy it.
